WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:02.877
- Multiple credit cards, high balances,

00:00:02.877 --> 00:00:05.714
high interest rates, high stress levels.

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:08.466
You've been making payments
over a long period of time,

00:00:08.466 --> 00:00:11.678
but it doesn't seem to have
put a dent in your debt.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.597
Perhaps, you're even
considering the dreaded B word.

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.474
But, before you go that far,

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:20.270
you may be considering something
called debt consolidation.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.022
- What is debt consolidation?

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.356
It's simply taking two

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.734
or more accounts and
combining them into one.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.360
And, that's where you'd
make your payments.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.278
- Well, that sounds good.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:30.697
Simplifying makes things easier right?

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.781
Not always

00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:34.409
- Consolidating your debt
may mean less paperwork,

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:37.495
but that doesn't mean it's
the best path out the woods.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:40.623
- There are several different
ways to combine your balances

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:43.209
and you should understand
the good and bad of each

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.754
before you decide what's right for you.

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.339
(lively music)

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:56.056
- One way to consolidate debt

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.017
is to simply transfer the
balance from one credit card

00:00:59.017 --> 00:00:59.851
to another.

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:02.604
Credit card companies are
often happy to do this

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:04.981
since it means you'll
get in deeper with them.

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:07.650
Many will offer a variety of promotions,

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.738
0% APR over the course of
anywhere between 12 to 18 months.

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.990
Some will offer an
extended promotion date,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.242
but at a slightly higher interest rate.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.078
Transfer fees are common.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.121
So, be sure to factor that in.

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:21.998
- This sounds like a pretty simple way

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:23.625
to get some immediate relief,

00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:26.294
but beware of the fine print.

00:01:26.294 --> 00:01:29.464
Most of these deals
involve deferred interest

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:31.633
which means that you're
still accruing interest

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:34.636
on your balance during the
whole promotional period.

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:36.096
When the promotion expires,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.848
you are charged all of
that accumulated interest

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:41.309
despite the number of
payments you've made.

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:42.310
Yikes.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.812
- Another way to consolidate debt

00:01:43.812 --> 00:01:45.688
is through a personal loan.

00:01:45.688 --> 00:01:47.190
You get a loan from a bank,

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.109
use it to pay off all your credit cards,

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.152
and then make payments to the bank.

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:52.153
Sounds simple.

00:01:52.153 --> 00:01:54.322
Again, there are some hitches.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:56.116
- First of all, your credit has to be

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:59.077
in a favorable condition
to actually get approved.

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:00.787
If you've been struggling to make payments

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:01.913
on multiple cards,

00:02:01.913 --> 00:02:03.164
which you probably are

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:04.958
if you're considering consolidation,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.127
then it'll be pretty hard to get a loan.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:10.046
And, even if you do, the
terms probably won't be great.

00:02:10.046 --> 00:02:11.714
This route only makes sense

00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:14.425
if you can get a lower APR on the loan

00:02:14.425 --> 00:02:16.136
than you have on the cards.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:19.180
- Also, this method can
be very risky for someone

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:22.142
who has trouble restraining
their urge to spend.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.978
Suddenly having several
wide open credit cards

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.354
may be too much temptation.

00:02:26.354 --> 00:02:28.773
There are many cases where consumers

00:02:28.773 --> 00:02:31.651
have taken out a loan to pay
off all their credit card debt

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:34.821
just to turn around and run
the cards right back up.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.991
- The third option is to
seek the help of a company

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.618
that specializes in debt settlement.

00:02:40.618 --> 00:02:42.787
It may sound attractive
to let someone else

00:02:42.787 --> 00:02:44.289
handle all the messy details,

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:46.958
but you should definitely
know how it works.

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:50.003
- First, they ask you to
stop paying all your debts

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:52.046
and instead start making payments

00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:54.257
into a special savings account.

00:02:54.257 --> 00:02:56.926
Once there's enough there,
they take that money

00:02:56.926 --> 00:03:00.180
and negotiate a payoff with
each of your creditors,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.308
typically much lower than
the full amount you owe them.

00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:05.476
So, what are the downsides?

00:03:05.476 --> 00:03:08.062
- First, their fee, which can be as high

00:03:08.062 --> 00:03:11.274
as 25% of your total debt.

00:03:11.274 --> 00:03:14.485
Second, since you're effectively
defaulting on your loans,

00:03:14.485 --> 00:03:16.946
your credit score will get hammered.

00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:19.782
And, third, they may
not even be successful.

00:03:19.782 --> 00:03:21.492
If they can't reach an agreement

00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:23.369
with one or more of your creditors,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.830
you'll still be on the
hook for the full amount

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.125
with all the fees and
damage to your credit.

00:03:29.125 --> 00:03:31.836
- Maybe, none of these sound
like great options to you.

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:33.421
Well, there's good news.

00:03:33.421 --> 00:03:36.341
Many people actually have greater success

00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:38.885
by not consolidating their debt.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.930
It may sound nice to
simplify your payments,

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.725
but the psychological effect
of having one giant loan

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.727
can be very intimidating.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.521
At a time when you need
discipline and optimism,

00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:53.358
you feel discouraged and hopeless.

00:03:53.358 --> 00:03:55.318
- By keeping debts separate

00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:57.445
and focusing on one at a time,

00:03:57.445 --> 00:04:00.031
you can get a feeling of
accomplishment and pride

00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:01.574
with each closed account,

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:04.285
which can go a long way
to keeping you motivated.

00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:08.206
It's all about knowing what
works best for your personality.

00:04:08.206 --> 00:04:10.208
- If you decide to keep
your debts separate,

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.585
you can negotiate directly
with your creditors

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:13.836
for some leniency,

00:04:13.836 --> 00:04:16.464
often called hardship programs.

00:04:16.464 --> 00:04:19.217
These policies were
developed to assist consumers

00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:22.428
that are struggling with
making on time payments.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.556
If qualified, the creditors
will lower your monthly payment

00:04:25.556 --> 00:04:26.808
and interest rate,

00:04:26.808 --> 00:04:28.351
no defaulted accounts,

00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:30.520
no wasted money paying a company

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.605
to do what you can do yourself.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.524
But, there are some hurdles.

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:35.692
- You may have to prove

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:38.194
that you are actually facing a hardship.

00:04:38.194 --> 00:04:40.321
Shop-aholism doesn't count.

00:04:40.321 --> 00:04:43.491
Think family emergencies,
job losses, pay cuts,

00:04:43.491 --> 00:04:44.951
or medical illness,

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.495
and you may need
documentation to prove it.

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:48.496
Once in the program,

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:51.749
the lender will either close
or freeze your account.

00:04:51.749 --> 00:04:54.002
They may also lower your credit limit.

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:57.255
If this results in a high
utilization percentage,

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.257
the proportion between what you owe

00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:00.717
and the total you can borrow,

00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:03.928
you are likely to see a
decrease in your scores.

00:05:03.928 --> 00:05:04.762
- In the end,

00:05:04.762 --> 00:05:07.473
there's no one right way to handle debt.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.100
The important thing is that you know

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.435
what you're getting into

00:05:10.435 --> 00:05:12.228
and that you know yourself

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:14.814
- Your personal strengths and weaknesses

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.150
will determine how well
each option would work.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.111
So, you need to take an
honest look at yourself

00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:21.571
before making a decision.

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:24.115
- [All] And, that's our two cents.

